## ls -a

```bash
ls -a
```
Shows hidden files too. Hidden = name starts with `.` (**dotfiles**).

```bash
ls -A
```
Almost all: hidden files but without `.` and `..`.

```bash
ls -al
```
Options combined: all files + long format.

```bash
ls .
```
`.` = current directory. Same output as plain `ls`.

```bash
ls ..
```
`..` = parent directory. Lists the folder above.

