## Time style

```bash
ls -l --time-style=iso
ls -l --time-style=long-iso
ls -l --time-style=full-iso
```
Only changes how the date column looks.

| Style | Looks like |
|-------|-----------|
| locale (default) | `Oct 31 11:33` |
| iso | `10-31 11:33` |
| long-iso | `2026-10-31 11:33` |
| full-iso | `2026-10-31 11:33:27.488202626 +0000` |

Date codes (same as `date`): `%Y` year, `%m` month, `%d` day, `%H` hour, `%M` minute, `%S` second, `%N` nanoseconds, `%z` timezone offset.

```bash
ls -l --time-style="+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M"
ls --full-time
```
Custom format / shortcut for `-l --time-style=full-iso`.

